 "text": "The slot holds the head `prototypes + sentences` for `tinyclip-39m-16` (species_taxon_com, beta 8, bias for species without photos 0.8), fitted on `images/alachua-2025 (two thirds of val)`, with 5911 species rows, and a bias a row. Every photo's vector (`images/alachua-2025.wasm-int8-per-channel`) went through `tools/fusion/fuse.py`, the reference of the page's arithmetic, with the slot's own files as the page reads them (half-precision rows). Settings: rule `product`, t_kind 20, w_kind 0.7, alpha_prior 1. On 565 tuning photos (the third of val kept for tuning) the thresholds came out as name_at 0.89 and offer_at 0.94. On the 4197 test photos the kind of eye is right for 87.0% (85.9 to 88.0); the top species is right for 36.3% (34.9 to 37.8) and is among the first five for 58.8% (57.2 to 60.2). `person` was said for 0.02% of these photos and `none` for 0.02%; the set holds neither. The top species from fuse.py differs from a direct matrix computation on the same files for 0 photos. The kinds head is `kind phrases`. With kind_at 0.46 (set on wildlife tuning photos alone, because the extra set's vectors were not published for this model), the page asserts a kind for 77.7% (76.4 to 79.0) of the wildlife test photos and is right for 95.4% (94.7 to 96.1) of those; for the 22.3% (21.0 to 23.6) where it is not sure, the true kind is among its three likeliest for 91.4% (89.7 to 93.3). The slot needs: species.bias_url (build 7 of the page); fusion.kind_at (the build of the page that has the answer `not sure`).",
